MID_SE_Bon_Ned_C: <EDH>
MID_SE_Bon_Ned_C_001: That is all you need to know of your duties. I look\nforward to seeing you fight on our side.
MID_SE_Bon_Ned_C_002: Yes, sir. It's just...
MID_SE_Bon_Ned_C_003: What is it? You have some misgivings?
MID_SE_Bon_Ned_C_004: There's something I don't understand.
MID_SE_Bon_Ned_C_005: You are loyal to Queen Theodora above everything\nelse, and yet here I am. Like nothing happened.
MID_SE_Bon_Ned_C_006: You know I once served a Dyanist house.
MID_SE_Bon_Ned_C_007: Then you personally convey the details of the\nassignment to me, a lowly mercenary. Why?
MID_SE_Bon_Ned_C_008: You lost the house you served and left your country.\nI judge that you pose no threat to us.
MID_SE_Bon_Ned_C_009: But I might rise through the ranks here, then return\nto Saramis only to fan the flames of rebellion again.
MID_SE_Bon_Ned_C_010: Hehe. An interesting hypothetical. I am well\naware of your character, Nydine.
MID_SE_Bon_Ned_C_011: I know that you carry out your assignments\nscrupulously and are ever honing your skills.
MID_SE_Bon_Ned_C_012: You are swayed not by houses or politics, but devote\nyourself entirely to the battle at hand.
MID_SE_Bon_Ned_C_013: I sincerely doubt you would exact revenge on Her\nMajesty at this juncture.
MID_SE_Bon_Ned_C_014: You're right. I would never even consider it.
MID_SE_Bon_Ned_C_015: Putting aside your former allegiance to Dyan's\nfaction, you are a paragon of a Saraminian warrior.
MID_SE_Bon_Ned_C_016: That is what I see when I look at you. Even in your\nrole as a mercenary, I can tell what drives you.
MID_SE_Bon_Ned_C_017: Mercenaries whose allegiances are based on money\nwill turn on you for money. You are not one such.
MID_SE_Bon_Ned_C_018: I have been known to turn down a job if I think it's\nunjust or suspect. Money isn't everything to me.
MID_SE_Bon_Ned_C_019: Exactly. You respect justice and seek to become a\nstronger warrior. I find that laudable in a soldier.
MID_SE_Bon_Ned_C_020: I'm shocked you think so highly of me, Commander.
MID_SE_Bon_Ned_C_021: Actually, I have had an interest in you as a warrior\nfor some time.
MID_SE_Bon_Ned_C_022: I daresay I am not alone. Many of our troops still\nadore you.
MID_SE_Bon_Ned_C_023: I have been hoping to see you in our camp, bravely\nraising morale and showing off your prowess.
MID_SE_Bon_Ned_C_024: That's very kind. To be completely honest, this\nis all coming out of the blue.
MID_SE_Bon_Ned_C_025: I always figured you for a logical man, Commander\nBonaventure. One who avoided unnecessary risks.
MID_SE_Bon_Ned_C_026: So now you see there is a human behind the wizened\ncommander, who cannot help but follow his instincts.
MID_SE_Bon_Ned_C_027: Indeed. Consider my doubts erased. I'll keep on\nfighting and grow as strong as I can.
MID_SE_Bon_Ned_C_028: As a once proud warrior of Saramis.
MID_SE_Bon_Ned_C_029: I can say, as one of those very warriors, that I look\nforward to it.